      "content": "calling it a \"legal fiction\" seems pretty extreme though. don't you think that dismisses the entire constitutional framework of the separation of powers? if the executive can just claim privilege whenever they want to avoid oversight, doesn't that basically turn the presidency into an unchecked power, which is exactly what the founders were trying to prevent?",
